0	section	The Dying Tree
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	Welcome Traveller. I am King Narnode. It's nice to see an outsider.
1	line	Player	Hi! It seems to be a busy settlement.
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	For now.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	You seem worried, what's up?
2	line	Player	You seem worried, what's up?
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	Traveller, can I speak to you in strictest confidence?
2	line	Player	Of course sire.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	Not here, follow me.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	Down here.
1	option	I'll be off now.
2	line	Player	I'll be off now.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	Enjoy your stay with us. There are many things to see in my kingdom.
2	action	end
0	section	Foundations cutscene
1	line	Player	So what is this place?
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	These, my friend, are the foundations of the stronghold.
1	line	Player	They look like roots to me.
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	Not just any roots Traveller! These were created by gnome mages eons ago, since then they have grown to become a mighty stronghold!
1	line	Player	Impressive. What exactly is the problem?
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	In the last two months our tree guardians have reported continuing deterioration of the Grand Tree's health. I've never seen this before! It could be the end for us all!
1	line	Player	You mean the tree is ill?
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	In effect yes. Would you be willing to help us discover what is happening to the tree?
1	cond	If the player is below level 50 combat:
2	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that your combat level is lower than the recommended level of 50.
1	select	Start The Grand Tree quest?
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	I'd be happy to help!
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	Thank Guthix for your arrival!
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	The first task is to find out what's killing the tree.
2	line	Player	Do you have an idea?
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	My top tree guardian, Glough, believes it's human sabotage. I'm not so sure! The only way to know for sure is to talk to Hazelmere.
2	line	Player	Who's Hazelmere?
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	Hazelmere is one of the mages that created the Grand Tree! He is the only one that has survived from that time. Take this bark sample to him, he will be able to help!
2	box	The king shows you a sample of bark.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	The mage only talks in the old tongue, you'll need this.
2	box	The king shows you a translation book.
2	line	Player	What is it?
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	It's a translation book, you'll need it to translate what Hazelmere says. Do that carefully! His words are our only hope! You'll find his dwellings high upon a towering hill, on an island east of Yanille.
2	box	The king hands you the bark sample and the translation book.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	I'll show you the way back up.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	Up here.
2	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	I'm sorry, I don't want to get involved.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	I understand Traveller. Please keep this to yourself.
2	line	Player	Of course.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	I'll show you the way back up.
2	line	King Narnode Shareen	Up here.
2	action	end
