0	section	Interrogating the Prisoner
1	line	Player	Tell me. Why would you want to kill the Grand Tree?
1	line	Charlie	What do you mean?!
1	line	Player	Don't tell me, you just happened to be caught carrying Daconia rocks!
1	line	Charlie	All I know is that I did what I was asked.
1	line	Player	I don't understand.
1	line	Charlie	Glough paid me to go to this gnome on a hill. I gave the gnome a seal and he gave me some rocks to give to Glough.
1	line	Charlie	I've been doing it for weeks, this time though Glough locked me up here! I just don't understand it.
1	line	Player	Sounds like Glough is hiding something!
1	line	Charlie	I don't know what he's up to. If you want to find out you'd better search his home.
1	line	Player	Okay. Thanks Charlie.
1	line	Charlie	Good luck!
1	action	end
0	section	When talking to Charlie again
1	line	Player	Hello Charlie.
1	line	Charlie	Hello adventurer. Have you figured out what's going on?
1	line	Player	No idea.
1	line	Charlie	To get to the bottom of this you'll need to search Glough's home.
1	action	end
0	section	Reporting back to King Narnode
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	Hello Traveller. So, did you speak to the culprit?
1	line	Player	Yes I did and something's not right!
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	What do you mean?
1	line	Player	The prisoner said he was paid by Glough to get the Daconia stones!
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	That's absurd! He's just trying to save himself!
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	Since Glough's wife died he's been a little strange. He would never wrongly imprison someone though! Now that the culprit is locked up we can relax. It's sad but I think Glough was right.
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	Humans are planning to invade and wipe out the tree gnomes!
1	line	Player	But why?
1	line	King Narnode Shareen	Who knows? You may have to leave soon Traveller! I trust you but the local gnomes are getting paranoid.
1	action	end
0	section	When talking to King Narnode again
